==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Nefer Aset''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Almighty Aset''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
At first glance, this unit seems extremely lackluster. Although she has relatively high health, 300 standing range and 3.5k base DPS is very low - even non-Uber midrangers can replicate this number and easily surpass it with stacking. [[Wave Attack]] effectively doubles her DPS as nearly all enemies hit by her initial attack will also be hit by her Wave, giving her 7k DPS, and her [[Strengthen]] also gives +50% DMG at 2/3 health, which brings her DPS up to 10.5k, making her DMG comparable to [[Togeluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Togelan Pasalan]] and [[Mighty Rekon Korps (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Rekon Korps]], two great generalist DPS options while also boasting a much quicker 111s recharge.

Lightmother Aset has really good mobility, with decent cost, short cooldown, fast speed, and a long enough backswing for clipping to not be a concern. Her Wave Attacks combined with an extremely fast attack cycle make her amazing at clearing peons. This gives Aset great synergy with powerful [[:Category:Single Attack Cats|single-target attackers]], such as [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]. Her only real weaknesses are very low standing range and lack of a good niche, as most [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus enemies]] outrange her and can inflict status effects, which she is powerless against. Her low standing range can be considered a weakness against aggressive enemies, though she has plenty of health to somewhat mitigate this.

==='''True Form'''===
Almighty Aset's most prominent gains include an HP boost, range increase and two immunities.

Her new standing range of 350 is immediately a massive boost to her survivability, being able to outrange a few more notable midrangers such as [[M. Ost]], [[Rain D.]] and [[Midnite D.]] However, the biggest difference this makes is giving her the privilege to outrange [[Baron Seal]], albeit only by 30 range. This finally gives her Colossus Slayer niche more of an actual purpose, since she was previously outranged by every Colossus [[Gauntlet]] boss save for [[Archangel Exiel]], and [[Immune to Freeze|Immunity to Freeze]] is another nifty bonus against Baron Seal. Given her absurdly high Strengthened DPS against Colossus enemies, this niche expansion is more than welcome even if small.

On the flip side, [[Immune to Toxic]] is arguably the more consequential of the two immunities she gets. She becomes an optimal counter to [[Big Peng Z]], with him being able to activate her Strengthen ability naturally over time without ever putting her in any real danger. Even putting aside Colossus enemies, she serves as a decent counter against other [[:Category:Enemies with Toxic ability|Toxic enemies]] such as [[Gobble]], [[Zollow]], and even [[Heavenly Herald Papuu]].

The HP boost is just the cherry on top, since she can now activate her Strengthen at a less worrisome threshold. It is worth noting that even with these improvements, her performance in general is still just ''okay''. Many of her already existing matchups/interactions remain fairly unchanged outside of the ones mentioned, and she's still just as finicky to use ideally.

